│  empirical validation rest primarily on a single paper, `tot_2023`, though   │
│  corroborated taxonomically by `wang_2023_survey`).                          │
│                                                                              │
│  ---                                                                         │
│                                                                              │
│  #### Theme 3: Episodic verbal reflection and structured memory streams      │
│  enable non-parametric behavioral adaptation.                                │
│  * **Claim:** Agents can systematically self-correct and maintain            │
│  longitudinal behavioral coherence across tasks without gradient weight      │
│  updates by converting environmental signals into natural language           │
│  reflections and storing them in structured memory modules.                  │
│  * **Evidence:**                                                             │
│    * `reflexion_2023`: Demonstrates that converting scalar/binary            │
│  environmental feedback into natural language summaries provides a           │
│  "semantic gradient" that agents use as context in subsequent trials,        │
│  yielding double-digit performance gains across AlfWorld, HotpotQA, and      │
│  HumanEval.                                                                  │
│    * `generative_agents_2023`: Establishes an architecture based on a        │
│  comprehensive memory stream, score-based retrieval (recency, importance,    │
│  relevance), and recursive reflection to generate coherent, long-term        │
│  autonomous behaviors.                                                       │
│    * `wang_2023_survey`: Categorizes memory recollection and planning with   │
